event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":102,"item_id":"rs_01b345bfb0a9a539016aca1bb041bc8195b2119487e3ca1d89","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Implementing server-side forms**\n\nI need to implement some simple server-side rendering (SSR) forms with native browser labels. The easiest way involves full navigation, form posting, and handling redirects for any errors like blank fields being visible. I’ll use Node with an HTTP spawn for persistence and a built-in SQLite database for creating a default directory and data. The route setup includes POST for projects and GET for pages. I should also ensure 404 errors are handled gracefully. Testing could involve using a random port for ease of capture."}

event: response.reasoning_summary_part.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","sequence_number":103,"item_id":"rs_01b345bfb0a9a539016aca1bb041bc8195b2119487e3ca1d89","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Implementing server-side forms**\n\nI need to implement some simple server-side rendering (SSR) forms with native browser labels. The easiest way involves full navigation, form posting, and handling redirects for any errors like blank fields being visible. I’ll use Node with an HTTP spawn for persistence and a built-in SQLite database for creating a default directory and data. The route setup includes POST for projects and GET for pages. I should also ensure 404 errors are handled gracefully. Testing could involve using a random port for ease of capture."}}

